  "notes": [
    "Reflexive compound of *volver* — follows the same irregular patterns.",
    "o→ue stem change in the stressed syllables: presente (all but nosotros/nosotras) and subjuntivo presente (all but nosotros/nosotras). Nosotros/nosotras reverts to the unstressed stem (nos volvemos, nos volvamos).",
    "No stem change in the pretérito indefinido — regular -ER endings throughout (me volví, se volvió...).",
    "Irregular past participle, inherited from *volver→vuelto*: **vuelto**.",
    "Imperativo afirmativo reflexive pronouns attach to the end with a written accent to preserve stress (vuélvete, vuélvase, volvámonos, vuélvanse); imperativo negativo places them separately in front (no te vuelvas...).",
    "Used for a change of state (like \"to become,\" similar to *ponerse* and *hacerse*, but usually for more permanent or drastic changes): *volverse loco* (\"to go crazy\").",
    "*Los personajes cruzan la línea... de pronto se vuelve impredecible.* (\"The reality suddenly becomes unpredictable.\")",
    "*Se volvió muy desconfiado después de eso.* (\"He became very distrustful after that.\")",
    "Related: *volver* (non-reflexive, \"to return / to do again\"), *convertirse en* (near-synonym, more gradual \"to become/turn into\"), *ponerse* (near-synonym, for temporary emotional/physical states)."
  ],
